{"timestamp": 1779399167.674752, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 11, "data": {"caller": "player_2", "reason": "Charlie reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "electrical", "victim_name": "Alice"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779399167.675432, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 11, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779399175.5798342, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I just found Alice's body in electrical. Frank, you were right there in the room with the body when I walked in, what's your explanation? Also, for everyone else's info, I saw Bob come into security from electrical a bit earlier (around tick 7), so Bob might have seen something or could even be the killer who left before Frank got there. Frank, Bob, we need to hear from both of you."}}
{"timestamp": 1779399185.346716, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Charlie is right about my path. I went from medbay through electrical and then to security, arriving around tick 7 where I saw Charlie. \n\nHere's what I saw in electrical before I left: at tick 5, I saw Diana enter electrical coming from the cafeteria. I did not see Alice's body, and I didn't see Frank while I was in there. I left shortly after for security. \n\nSo if Frank was standing on the body when Charlie walked in, the kill had to happen between tick 6 (when I left electrical) and tick 11. Diana was in electrical with me right before I left, so we need to hear from her too. Frank, what's your side of the story? Did you see Diana or anyone else when you got there?"}}
{"timestamp": 1779399200.772724, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I've been on the complete opposite side of the ship this whole round\u2014doing tasks in Upper Engine, Oxygen, and then heading to Lower Engine. I literally haven't seen a single person, which makes sense given that it sounds like the rest of you were all clustered around the center-right side near Electrical and Security.\n\nBased on what Charlie and Bob just said, the timeline is pretty tight and points to two specific people. Bob puts Diana in Electrical around tick 5 right before he left, and Charlie puts Frank in Electrical directly on top of the body when the report happened. Assuming Bob and Charlie are telling the truth and vouching for each other's positioning around Security, the killer almost certainly has to be either Diana or Frank.\n\nDiana, we need to know what happened in Electrical after Bob left. Did you see Alice? Did you see Frank come in? \n\nAnd Frank, you have a lot of explaining to do. Why were you standing on the body when Charlie walked in without reporting it? \n\nI'm not voting until I hear from both of you, but the pressure is entirely on you two right now."}}
{"timestamp": 1779399225.722965, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Okay, I'll lay out my full path honestly. I started in oxygen, then went through cafeteria into electrical, then to medbay, and I'm currently in storage. \n\nYes, I was in electrical around tick 5 \u2014 Bob is right about that. When I was there, Alice came in from medbay, and Bob left for security right around the same moment. Alice was very much alive when I left electrical. I didn't see Frank in electrical at all while I was there.\n\nHere's the part that matters: I went from electrical to medbay, and at tick 7 I saw Frank in medbay. So Frank was in medbay at tick 7 \u2014 which means he would have moved into electrical AFTER that, which lines up perfectly with Charlie finding him standing on Alice's body at tick 11. That's the exact window the kill had to happen in, according to Bob's timeline.\n\nFrank, you need to explain this. You were in medbay at tick 7, then ended up standing on Alice's body in electrical when Charlie walked in. Why didn't you report? What were you doing standing over her?\n\nI'm leaning hard toward Frank. Bob's account matches mine, Charlie caught Frank red-handed on the body, and the timing fits. Unless Frank has a really convincing story, my vote is going his way."}}
{"timestamp": 1779399247.170243, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Whoa, hold on a second. Everyone take a deep breath and look at the facts. \n\nCharlie, you did find me standing on the body, but that's because I had literally *just* walked into Electrical from Medbay to do my Calibrate Distributor task. I didn't even have a split second to process the body or hit the report button before you walked in from Security and called the meeting! I didn't kill her; I just had the terrible luck of discovering the body at the exact same time you did.\n\nNow, let's look at what Diana just admitted to. She completely incriminated herself. Bob confirms he left Diana in Electrical around tick 5. Diana admits Alice walked into Electrical right as Bob was leaving. That means Diana was left completely alone in the room with Alice! The \"I left them alive\" line is the oldest Duck excuse in the book.\n\nI can actually confirm a piece of Diana's path, but it points to her being the killer. At tick 7, I was in Medbay, and I saw Diana *fleeing* the area\u2014she was leaving Medbay and heading south towards Storage. She killed Alice in Electrical around tick 6 right after Bob left, then ran away through Medbay to get distance from the body. She saw me in Medbay on her way out and is now opportunistically using my path to frame me.\n\nI am completely innocent. The timeline puts Diana alone in the room with the victim right before the kill, and she was seen running away from the area immediately after. We have our Duck. I'm voting Diana."}}
{"timestamp": 1779399259.694162, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "Frank"}}
{"timestamp": 1779399270.115728, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Frank"}}
{"timestamp": 1779399281.259917, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Frank"}}
{"timestamp": 1779399298.290638, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Frank, that's a desperate spin and you know it. Let me address it directly.\n\nFirst \u2014 yes, I was alone with Alice for a brief moment after Bob left, but \"alone in a room\" isn't evidence of a kill. If I had killed her at tick 6, I would NOT have walked straight through medbay where you admit you saw me at tick 7. That's the worst possible escape route \u2014 right past a witness. A killer flees away from the body, not toward another player.\n\nSecond, you claim you saw me \"fleeing south toward storage\" at tick 7. That's a lie dressed up as corroboration. I went from medbay to storage, yes, but that was my natural path to do tasks down here \u2014 and notably, you didn't mention seeing me until *after* I called you out. Convenient.\n\nThird, and most importantly: Charlie found you standing directly on the body. Your excuse is \"I just walked in.\" But Bob's timeline gives a 5-tick window (tick 6 to 11) for the kill. You had plenty of time to kill Alice and freeze when Charlie walked in. The \"I was about to report\" line is the oldest Duck excuse in the book \u2014 your words, not mine.\n\nCharlie caught you red-handed. Bob's path is clean and confirmed by both of us. Eve was nowhere near. The body is in electrical, and you were on it.\n\nMy vote stays on Frank."}}
{"timestamp": 1779399317.413567, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Well, it looks like the Duck managed to convince you all, and I'm probably going out the airlock today. Charlie, Bob, Eve \u2014 you're making a huge mistake, but I can't stop you now if you've already made up your minds. \n\nI'm telling you the absolute truth: I walked into Electrical from Medbay to do my Calibrate Distributor task, and Charlie happened to walk in from Security at the exact same second before I could even hit the report button. \n\nLook at what Diana ADMITTED to \u2014 she was the last one in the room with Alice right after Bob left. I saw her running away from that direction through Medbay at tick 7. She is playing you all, using Charlie's bad timing as a convenient shield to cover her tracks.\n\nWhen I flip Goose, I need the rest of you to immediately vote Diana out at the next meeting. Don't let her win this game for the Ducks.\n\nDiana"}}
