{"timestamp": 1779399708.15263, "event_type": "tick_start", "tick": 32, "data": {"tick": 32}}
{"timestamp": 1779399714.4526982, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 32, "data": {"caller": "player_1", "reason": "Bob reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "security", "victim_name": "Eve"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779399714.453866, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 32, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779399727.1067038, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 32, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I just found Eve dead in security. My path this round was pretty long: upper engine, up to oxygen, back down to upper engine, lower engine, storage, navigation, and finally into security where I found the body. \n\nI haven't seen either of you (Charlie or Diana) this entire round since the last meeting. Since Frank was ejected and the game hasn't ended, that means Frank was innocent and the last duck is one of you two. We're at the final three, so whoever we vote for decides the game. \n\nCharlie, Diana \u2014 where have you both been this round? Did either of you cross paths, or did either of you see Eve before she died? Please be detailed, we need to get this right."}}
{"timestamp": 1779399738.559018, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 32, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "Bob, your route is incredibly long. For my part, I've been making my way around the left side of the map mostly\u2014doing tasks in electrical, engines, oxygen, storage, and I was just working on my medbay scan when the meeting was called. I haven't crossed paths with you or Diana since the last meeting, and the last time I saw Eve was way back at tick 13 in electrical. \n\nSince I know I'm innocent, it comes down to you or Diana. Bob, finding the body in security after such a massive trek across the map is a bit suspicious, but I want to hear from Diana before I make up my mind. Diana, where were you this entire round? Did you see anyone? We need your full path because this vote decides the game. I won't vote until we hear her side."}}
{"timestamp": 1779399774.687066, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 32, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Okay, here's my round \u2014 I worked the right side of the map. I started in navigation and did the chart task there, then cut up through security toward weapons. I was in security only briefly, passing through, and I didn't see Eve in there when I went through \u2014 though I'll admit I wasn't lingering. From weapons I went into cafeteria, then down to electrical to do wiring, and finished on a medbay scan. So Charlie and I basically had mirror-image routes \u2014 him on the left, me on the right \u2014 which is probably why we never crossed.\n\nNow let me be honest about what's bothering me. Charlie, you and I were each working one half of the map cleanly. Bob's route is the outlier \u2014 upper engine, oxygen, back to upper engine, lower engine, storage, navigation, AND security? That's nearly every room on the ship. That's not a task route, that's a hunting route. And he conveniently ends it by \"finding\" Eve in security \u2014 the reporter is almost always the killer in a setup like this.\n\nAlso, Bob, you said you went through navigation right before security. I was in navigation earlier in the round and didn't see you pass through. If your route was real and that long, our timing should have overlapped somewhere on the right side, and it didn't.\n\nCharlie, I know you said you wanted to hear me out before deciding. I'm telling you straight: I'm voting Bob. His route covers the murder location, he's the reporter, and his story is the only one that doesn't fit the geometry of the map. If we split, the duck wins by default. I need you with me on Bob."}}
